# Use pnpm for Package Management

Always use `pnpm` instead of `npm` or `yarn` when installing, updating, or managing dependencies in this project.

## Rules:
- Use `pnpm add <package>` instead of `npm install <package>`
- Use `pnpm add -D <package>` for dev dependencies instead of `npm install -D <package>`
- Use `pnpm remove <package>` instead of `npm uninstall <package>`
- Use `pnpm update` instead of `npm update`
- Use `pnpm run <script>` instead of `npm run <script>`

## Examples:
- ✅ `pnpm add react`
- ✅ `pnpm add -D typescript`
- ✅ `pnpm remove lodash`
- ✅ `pnpm run dev`
- ❌ `npm install react`
- ❌ `yarn add react`
